UWA Honours Thesis – Supplementary Materials - TRUNG HO HUYNH
Project Overview

This repository contains the supplementary materials associated with an Honours thesis investigating the formation processes of grinding-patch cross-sectional morphology through controlled experimentation. The project focuses on understanding how grinding duration and active-stone contact area influence surface morphological change on granite substrates.

Repository Contents
### 1. Experimental Data

####  DEMs.zip
- Contains Digital Elevation Models (DEMs) generated from photogrammetry  
- Exported as TIFF raster files     
- Used for terrain analysis (slope calculation) 
- Captured at every 20-minute intervals of all granite samples
+ Note: Due to GitHub file-size limitations, this .zip files cannot be previewed directly within the browser. 
 To view,  download this file by clicking on file within the repository and click the “Download raw file” 
 button located in the upper-right corner (next to the word Raw) of the GitHub file page.   
---

#### Speed_of_motor_in_experiment_1.zip
- Contains **motor performance data (RPM)**  
- Recorded at **0.1-second intervals**  
- Used to calculate **stroke counts**  
- Ensures **experimental consistency**
+ Note: Due to GitHub file-size limitations, this .zip files cannot be previewed directly within the browser. 
 To view,  download this file by clicking on file within the repository and click the “Download raw file” 
 button located in the upper-right corner (next to the word Raw) of the GitHub file page. 
---

#### Machine_working_video.zip
- Video documentation of the **mechanical apparatus
- Shows reciprocal grinding motion of the mechanical apparatus  
+ Note: Due to GitHub file-size limitations, this .zip files cannot be previewed directly within the browser. 
 To view,  download this file by clicking on file within the repository and click the “Download raw file” 
 button located in the upper-right corner of the GitHub file page. 
---

#### sketch_nov6b.ino 
- the Andruino IDE program written for the controlling of motor rotation, speed, direction and RPM count 
- Open this file within the IDE software for viewing 

---

### 2. Analytical Outputs

#### markdown_statistic_supplyment.html
- Generated using R / RMarkdown
- Contains statistical analysis procedure and outputs    
- Includes plots, regression and model results  
+ Note: Due to GitHub file-size limitations, this .html files cannot be previewed directly within the browser. 
 To view,  download this file by clicking on file within the repository and click the “Download raw file” 
 button located in the upper-right corner (next to the word Raw) of the GitHub file page. 
---

#### surface_code_for_analysis.R
- R script used for data processing and analysis for reproducibility   
- Includes:
  - DEM processing  
  - Slope calculations  
  - Statistical modelling  

---

This ensures reproducibility of all analytical results.
